  "known_open_evidence": [
    "RanPAC transfer has a six-replicate controlled-head confirmation but does not reproduce PETL or the original per-task Ridge schedule.",
    "The equal-budget comparison covers one fixed signed CountSketch and a six-seed truncated-SVD LoRanPAC control, but no learned sketch, Nyström, frequent-directions, or official end-to-end LoRanPAC pipeline.",
    "No second-backbone result is available.",
    "Whole-process memory has four paired repetitions but still only one Tesla T4 and one software stack.",
    "The M6 fixed-INT8 width sweep formally fails its 0.25-point accuracy-retention gate at width 20000; M7 localizes downstream amplification but does not establish causality or measure the spectral condition number.",
    "M11 adaptive precision passes at widths 10000 and 20000 but is based on one development seed and increases state and update time relative to fixed P2B.",
    "M11b same-byte scale refinement lowers local factor error but formally fails the width-20000 retention gate by 0.000115 percentage points; no further scale-rule search is authorized on this stream.",
    "M14 completes all 60 multi-seed equal-byte LoRanPAC units but formally fails its task-1 solver-residual gate; M15 closes the numerical mechanism without changing predictions or passing M14 retroactively.",
    "The legacy ImageNet-R split is not content-disjoint.",
    "The state-matched final artifact requires a clean source-locked rerun before it is primary final evidence."
  ]
